# Code owners for andara.valesordev.com.
#
# GitHub uses this to request review automatically. It is also the machine-readable
# form of CLAUDE.md §2's implementation boundary — with one important caveat, stated
# here rather than discovered later:
#
#   Every path below is owned by @solo-seven, because that is the only account with
#   write access. Claude Code and Cursor both push as it. GitHub cannot express
#   "this path belongs to the architecture lane and that one to the implementation
#   lane" when both lanes are the same user, so the lane split lives in the section
#   headings and comments. Treat those as the contract; treat the @solo-seven column
#   as GitHub bookkeeping.
#
# Consequence worth knowing: with a single owner who is also the author of every PR,
# GitHub will not request a review (you cannot review your own pull request). This
# file therefore documents and surfaces ownership; it does not gate anything. The
# `main` ruleset today has approvals=0 and require_code_owner_review=false, which is
# the correct setting for a solo repository — turning code-owner review ON with one
# collaborator would make every PR permanently unmergeable.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Default
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*                           @solo-seven

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Claude Code's lane — runs *around* the game: specify, build, ship, operate,
# observe. CLAUDE.md §2, tiebreaker rule 2.
#
# A change here from the implementation lane is the signal to stop and check.
# The zone.proto collision on 2026-09-09 is the worked example: AW-SRV-001 needed
# ZoneDefinition, the schema had not merged, and a second .proto was written. The
# field numbers happened to agree. Had they not, they would now be permanent
# under ADR-0002 with a log written against them.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The schema authority (ADR-0007). Field numbers here are permanent.
/docs/specs/protocol/       @solo-seven
/buf.gen.yaml               @solo-seven

# Generated from the above and committed (ADR-0007 rule 5). Never hand-edited;
# a diff here without a matching .proto diff means someone edited output.
/gen/                       @solo-seven

# Planning and decisions. Story status is frontmatter; BACKLOG.md is generated.
/docs/                      @solo-seven
/BACKLOG.md                 @solo-seven
/CLAUDE.md                  @solo-seven

# Infrastructure, automation, and the single automation surface (CLAUDE.md §9).
/deploy/                    @solo-seven
/scripts/                   @solo-seven
/.github/                   @solo-seven
/Makefile                   @solo-seven
/.golangci.yml              @solo-seven
/.editorconfig              @solo-seven
/.dockerignore              @solo-seven

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Cursor's lane — runs *in* the game. CLAUDE.md §2, tiebreaker rule 1.
#
# Application source and its tests. Claude Code writes contracts and test plans
# for these, never the implementations.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/cmd/                       @solo-seven
/server/                    @solo-seven
/admin/                     @solo-seven
/agents/                    @solo-seven
/client/                    @solo-seven
/go.mod                     @solo-seven
/go.sum                     @solo-seven
